  "gap_decomposition_fluid_baseline": {
    "total_orders": 8.263002330849512,
    "(a)_row_coefficient": "C enters kappa* linearly: changing C from 1 to Cmax(f,w) moves the gap by log10(Cmax) orders: mixture range log10(Cmax) in [-1.996, +0.176]; coefficient can remove at most ~2.0 orders (w=0 rows, transverse floor) and can add 0.18.",
    "(b)_bound_branch": "Feng-Geng-Luo 1810.06753 (Phase 3's Buchdahl source): text restricts to kappa>0 ('we will only focus on the case of kappa>0', Sec.IIA) and the 1e8 figure requires a FUTURE ~3 Msun NS (abstract/conclusions: typical NS gives 1e9; 1e8 only if a 3 Msun NS 'is observed in the future'). As published it constrains kappa<0 NOT AT ALL. Sign-blind alternative in the literature: Avelino 2012 existence-of-NS / fundamental-length l_f = sqrt(|kappa|) argument, quoted by Sham et al. as |8 pi kappa rho0| <~ 0.1 -- an |kappa| bound of the same 1e8 order. So factor (b) moves APPLICABILITY, not the order of magnitude: 0 orders of the numeric gap, all of its branch status.",
    "(c)_scaling": "kappa* = c^2 Cmax / GBAR is forced by dimensions: tidal gradient ~ c^2/|kappa| at fixed x, so r0* = sqrt(x kappa*) ~ sqrt(|kappa|). The remaining ~8.3 orders (fluid) / ~6.3-8.4 orders (mixture) are (c): no coefficient or branch factor in the audit touches the sqrt scaling."
